{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1270415-in-game-plots-other-than-direct-violence","id":1270415,"title":"In-Game Plots Other Than Direct Violence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-24T13:26:09-08:00","id":1270415,"title":"In-Game Plots Other Than Direct Violence","content":"I'm running (against my best judgement) a BNS MET Vampire LARP. Much of the advice I've received involves having NPC's plot against or with the PCs against other PCs. What does a non-direct violent plot involve.<br /> <br /> Example, Giovanni want to take over the city. Other than them having hordes of Ghosts help them take over by violence, I'm not sure what else they could do? Other than Praxis, you can't really unseat a Prince - it's not as if there's a vote every 4 years. Even if you remove his or her resources dots, it wouldn't really affect anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T19:57:46-08:00","id":1270500,"title":"","content":"You could attempt to unseat a Prince by proving they are unfit to rule. If their competence is called into question, the matter will often settle itself. Those beneath the Prince may drive him out of power (because a Prince who can't run a city is one that cannot protect its inhabitants). May even kill him, if other vampires think they can maneuver to take his place. Or else the Camarilla Archons might come in and dispose of the Prince, if he's proving terminally incapable of running the city. At which point a vacancy will open up for someone else to rise.<br /> <br /> This is the point where the Giovanni can attempt to capitalize on that vacancy. A Giovanni taking the role herself is unlikely to work in a Camarilla city. But they could attempt to see that a candidate of their choosing takes the seat instead. Preferably one that is amenable to Giovanni interests. Better yet, a new Prince that is a puppet under Giovanni control. Or at least a weak one, that won't pose as much a threat to Giovanni interests.<br /> <br /> Even if the Giovanni can't influence the ascension of a new Prince, they can perhaps stall it, and capitalize on the power vacuum (and concurrent Camarilla in-fighting) to make inroads in the city, strengthening Clan Giovanni's position.<br /> <br /> The key to accomplishing any of this non-violently is to be subtle, and to employ subtle pressure and &quot;attacks&quot;. Instead of having ghosts assault people, use them to spy on people, followed by exploiting the information. Camarilla pawns can be blackmailed...or led into traps, if the Giovanni (through intermediaries) lets slip just enough information to get Camarilla vampires to act, but not enough to avoid pitfalls. Like telling them where they can find something they really want...while neglecting to inform them that organized crime, rival vampires, or vampire hunters guard such things, and would take offense to the intrusion. The Giovanni never raise a finger themselves. They merely let other actors do the fighting for them. Keeping Giovanni hands clean is the key to success, because it's more productive to stay off the radar and uninvolved in conflicts.<br /> <br /> Another way is to target the financial interests of Camarilla vampires, and slowly eat away at them...from a business perspective. Never forget that the Giovanni are as much financial wizards as necromancers. Buy out companies, take ownership of properties, pull strings in city hall to get havens shut down or inconvenienced. Vampires are parasites on the economy and infrastructure, as well as on blood. Starve them out. A vampire in danger of losing everything will become desperate. Careless. Prone to making rash decisions and critical mistakes. Again, if you can get said Camarilla vampires to blame or suspect one another, all the better. But any weakness can be exploited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T16:59:48-08:00","id":1270978,"title":"","content":"Giovanni can't (officially) be involved in politics. At the foundation of the Camarilla, they declared true independence.<br /> <br /> But a Giovanni Family member (or extended Family) that was embraced as a different clan could theoretically be involved in politics, like becoming Prince of a city, or seneshal (and controlling the bits that the Giovanni need controlled)<br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Giovanni\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Giovanni</a><br /> But, all the Giovanni need is to come in, remind the Prince of their independence and request a small area to operate out of. They are merchants of the occult (something the PCs could use to their advantage) Then the Giovanni can operate in the city and (if needed) trade services for access to areas they are &quot;Investigating for ghostly activity&quot; Or if they're good enough, they could charge to investigate the regions that they want access to .<br /> <br /> Ghost are best for Spying and researching; gathering blackmail on vampires than they are for attacking, only one type of ghost really has the power to attack, and it's a high level power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}